    <body>

<!--include menu.txt -->

        <section class="hero">
            <div class="hero-text">
                <p class="eyebrow">
                    Sets &middot; Probability &middot; Description &middot; Inference
                </p>
                <h1 class="toc-head">
                    Introduction to Statistics and Probability
                </h1>
                <p class="hero-lead">
                    Course notes on sets, counting, and probability; on
                    describing nominal, ordinal, interval, and ratio data;
                    and on testing for differences with chi-square,
                    <i>z</i>, and <i>t</i> tests.
                </p>
                <p class="hero-actions">
                    <a class="button primary" href="#topics">
                        Browse the topics
                    </a>
                    <a class="button" href="https://github.com/gcallah/statistics">
                        View on GitHub
                    </a>
                </p>
            </div>
            <img class="hero-art" src="graphics/hero.svg"
                 width="560" height="400"
                 alt="A histogram under a normal curve, with the bands one, two, and three standard deviations from the mean shaded">
        </section>

        <figure class="feature-card quote-card">
            <figcaption>
                &ldquo;Be able to analyze statistics, which can be used to
                support or undercut almost any argument.&rdquo;
                <cite>Marilyn vos Savant</cite>
            </figcaption>
        </figure>

